<!--
  Robot configuration for the BIOBUZZ launcher bench.

  THIS IS NOT A ROBOT. It is a spare Control Hub with the launcher's two
  flywheel modules and the feeder on it, before they are bolted to a chassis.
  It exists so the launcher's numbers (which way it is wired, the speed each
  piece leaves at, how long the feeder runs) can be found at a bench while
  the build team has the robots.

  Like the robot configs, it ships inside the APK and appears in the Driver
  Station list as "robot_launcher_bench" as soon as the app is installed. The
  one manual step, once per hub: on the bench's Driver Station,
  Configure Robot -> robot_launcher_bench -> Activate. The Launcher Bench
  OpMode warns if some other configuration is active.

  WIRING, as the bench was built on 24 Oct 2026 - read before changing:
    feeder    motor port 1: BOTH feeder motors on one Y cable
    launcher  motor port 2: BOTH flywheel motors on one Y cable, one encoder
                            in encoder port 2 (only one of the pair can be)
  A Y cable means software sees ONE motor per port: every command reaches
  both motors, and the speed read is whichever motor's encoder is plugged
  in. The wheels turning opposite ways comes from how the motors are
  mounted and wired, not from code. If both wheels turn the same way, that
  is a wiring fix; no software setting can separate them. There is no
  per-wheel trim on this rig for the same reason.

  This differs from the robots, where launcher_left and launcher_right each
  have their own port and encoder (Expansion Hub 1 and 2, feeder on 3).

  Device names here must match org.firstinspires.ftc.teamcode.hardware.DeviceNames
  (the LAUNCHER_BENCH list). RobotConfigXmlTest fails the build if they disagree.
-->
<Robot type="FirstInspires-FTC">
    <LynxUsbDevice name="Control Hub Portal" serialNumber="(embedded)" parentModuleAddress="173">
        <LynxModule name="Control Hub" port="173">

            <!-- Both feeder motors, Y-cabled to one port. -->
            <goBILDA5202SeriesMotor name="feeder"   port="1" />

            <!-- Both flywheel motors, Y-cabled to one port; one encoder. -->
            <goBILDA5202SeriesMotor name="launcher" port="2" />

        </LynxModule>
    </LynxUsbDevice>
</Robot>
